created: "2026-07-28T16:19:39Z"
createdby: DBot
description: |-
  Executes an XQL query on the Cortex platform.
  When wait_for_results is set to true, polls every 10 seconds until results are available or timeout is reached, then returns the query results.
  Results are limited to a maximum of 1000 records. If the query specifies a larger LIMIT, it will be automatically reduced to 1000.
  IMPORTANT: If asked to visualize existing XQL execution results with a chart (widget / graph), you must first regenerate the query using the same method that produced the original query, adding only the visualization clause at the end of the query and nothing else, and reuse the execution ID of the original XQL run to avoid unnecessary query cost, since queries that differ only by optional `| view graph ...` suffixes return the same results.
display: Cortex - Run XQL Query
isdetailsoverridden: false
locked: false
name: CortexRunXQLQuery
